XB-Kidux-Ages: 8-16
XB-Kidux-Before: scratchjr
Description: Kidux learning module: Scratch, stories and games made with blocks
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This learning
 module is Scratch's own editor, the one children use at school, served on
 this computer and shown in Chromium, in the child's language, without the
 Scratch website's community. Its library of characters, backdrops and
 sounds comes from the Scratch Foundation's servers, so it needs the
 internet for them. A child saves their projects as files in their own
 folders, and opens them again from there.
 .
 Once it is installed, an adult switches it on for each child on the
 Modules page of the adult panel.
